WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.033
In this walkthrough we'll read the
settlement queue, and see what is due
to pay and receive, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:16.567
The Settlement List is the operations queue.
Every cash movement the system expects
appears here, on its way to being paid or received.

3
00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:27.467
Two columns answer the daily question. Direction says
whether the money is going out or coming in, and payment
date says when. Sorting on the date gives you what is due today.

4
00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:40.300
The list opens on the operational view, which is the one to work
from. It keeps backdated open items visible, and hides settled and
cancelled history so the queue only shows what still needs attention.

5
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:47.000
Switch to all history when you need the full
record, including everything already settled or cancelled.

6
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.400
And back to the working queue, which
is where the day is actually run from.

7
00:00:52.400 --> 00:01:01.967
The status filter narrows the queue further.
Typing a status shows only the items in that
state — projected, instructed, or settled.

8
00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:12.967
Settlements are selected with the checkbox on each row. A
selection can be carried straight through to the next step,
which is instructing them against a settlement instruction.

9
00:01:12.967 --> 00:01:21.700
Open Instruct Settlement takes the
selection with it, so you do not re-key
anything. That is the subject of the next walkthrough.

10
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:29.833
That completes Settlements and What Is Due. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
